[{"changes":["Ch1: null 배지였던 §Joy in Chains를 '1-2'로 수정 (§ 헤더는 뒤따르는 본문과 배지 공유)","Ch1: MSG '### A Love That Will Grow' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 3-6)","Ch1: MSG '### They Can't Imprison the Message' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 12-14)","Ch1: 배지 수정 6건 — '3-5'→'3-6', '6-8'→'7-8', '17'→'18-21', '19-21'→'18-21', '22-25'→'22-26', '26-30'→'27-30' (MSG 문단 구분 기준)","Ch1: 18-21을 2개 문단으로 분리하고 splits 선언 (합병 아님)","Ch1: 9-11 문단에 MSG 'Live a lover's life, circumspect and exemplary' 복원 — 'careful and exemplary' 추가","Ch1: 기존 invented 헤더 '§A Life Jesus Is Proud Of'를 § 문단으로 정식화 (배지 9-11, KO와 구조 일치)"],"chapter":1,"confirmations_needed":[],"merges":[],"msg_ranges":["1-2","1-2","3-6","3-6","7-8","9-11","9-11","12-14","12-14","15-17","18-21","18-21","22-26","27-30"],"paragraphs":["§Joy in Chains","What's up, Philippi crew! It's Paul and Tim, just a couple of guys on Jesus's squad, hitting you up. This is for all the Jesus followers in town, including the head honchos and the whole team. We're sending you major positive energy and peace from God the Father and our main man, Jesus.","§A Love That Will Grow","Every time I even *think* about you guys, I'm like, 'Thank you, God!' Seriously, every single time, it makes me want to pray for you, and I'm not even mad about it. I'm so stoked that you've been all-in with us, spreading the good news about Jesus since day one. I'm 100% sure that God, who started this awesome thing in you, is gonna see it through and give you a miraculous transformation on the day Jesus comes back.","And for real, I'm not just gassing you up. You guys are my ride-or-dies. You stuck with me when I was in jail, when I was on trial, and when I got out. You've been there for the whole crazy ride, and God's been super generous to us through it all. He knows I miss you guys like crazy. Sometimes I feel like I'm on the same wavelength as Jesus about you.","§A Life Jesus Is Proud Of","So, here's what I'm praying for you: that your love for each other just keeps leveling up. And not just that you love a lot, but that you love *smart*. You gotta use your brain and check your feelings so your love is the real deal, not just some mushy, fake stuff. Live a lover's life — careful and exemplary — a life that makes Jesus proud. A life that's producing all kinds of good stuff, making Jesus look good to everyone and getting them all in on praising God.","§They Can't Imprison the Message","Hey, so I gotta tell you, being in jail has had the total opposite effect of what my haters wanted. Instead of shutting me down, the message about Jesus has blown up! All the guards here, and pretty much everyone else, found out I'm locked up because of Jesus. That made them curious, and now they're learning all about him. And get this: most of the other Jesus followers here are way more confident than ever, and they're not afraid to talk about God and Jesus.","Now, it's true that some people are preaching about Jesus just because they see me out of the way and they want the spotlight. But others are doing it for the right reasons. One group is all about love; they know I'm here defending the message and they want to help. The other group is just being greedy, trying to get something for themselves now that I'm not around. Their motives are wrong. They see me as competition, so they think the worse it is for me, the better it is for them.","So what do I do? I've decided I don't really care what their motives are. Whether they're good, bad, or whatever, every time they open their mouths, they're talking about Jesus, so I'm just gonna cheer them on!","And I'm gonna keep on cheering, because I know how this is all gonna end. With your prayers and the help of Jesus's Spirit, everything he wants to do in me and through me is gonna get done. I can't wait to see what's next. I'm not worried about being embarrassed at all. In fact, everything that's happening to me in here is just making Jesus more famous, whether I live or die. They didn't shut me up; they gave me a bigger stage! If I'm alive, I'm Jesus's messenger; if I'm dead, I'm his prize. It's a win-win. I can't lose.","As long as I'm alive, I've got good work to do. If I had to choose right now, I don't know what I'd pick. It's a tough call! The thought of leaving this life and being with Jesus is awesome. Some days, that's all I want. But most days, because of what you guys are going through, I know it's better for me to stick around. So, I'm planning on being here for a while, to help you grow and be joyful in your faith. You can look forward to a big reunion when I come visit you again. We'll be praising Jesus and having a great time together.","In the meantime, live in a way that makes the message of Jesus look good. Don't let your actions depend on whether I'm there or not. You've got to be the same whether I'm there to see it myself or I hear about it from far away. Stand together, have one goal, and fight for people to trust in the good news. Don't back down or get scared by the opposition. Your courage and unity will show them that they're going to lose and you're going to win—and it's all because of God. There's more to this life than just trusting in Jesus. There's also suffering for him. And the suffering is just as much a gift as the trust. You're in the same fight you saw me go through, and you're getting an update on it in this letter."],"splits":[{"msg_range":"18-21","note":"MSG 18-21 한 문단을 가독성상 2개 Teenz 문단으로 분리 — para 10은 'So how am I to respond?/cheer them on', para 11은 'keep that celebration going/I can't lose'","paras":[10,11]}],"title":"Paul's Letter From Lock-Up","verseRanges":["1-2","1-2","3-6","3-6","7-8","9-11","9-11","12-14","12-14","15-17","18-21","18-21","22-26","27-30"]},{"changes":["Ch2: MSG '### He Took on the Status of a Slave' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 5-8)","Ch2: MSG '### Rejoicing Together' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 12-13)","Ch2: null 배지였던 §Think Like Jesus → '1-4', §God Lifted Him Up → '9-11'로 수정","Ch2: 배지 수정 2건 — '25-28'→'25-27', '29-30'→'28-30' (MSG 문단 구분 기준)","Ch2: 1-4 문단에 MSG 'if you have a heart, if you care' 복원 — 'if you care about anyone' 추가","Ch2: 9-11 문단 'even the ghosts of people long gone' → 'even those who died long ago and are buried' (MSG 'those long ago dead and buried'에 충실)","Ch2: 14-16 문단에 MSG 'Do everything readily and cheerfully'와 'Go out into the world uncorrupted' 복원","Ch2: KO의 invented 헤더 §별처럼 빛나라/§함께 기뻐해라와 구조 일치를 위해 EN에 §Shine Like Stars(14-16)/§Rejoice With Me(17-18) 추가"],"chapter":2,"confirmations_needed":[],"merges":[],"msg_ranges":["1-4","1-4","5-8","5-8","9-11","9-11","12-13","12-13","14-16","14-16","17-18","17-18","19-24","25-27","28-30"],"paragraphs":["§Think Like Jesus","So, if you've gotten anything good out of following Jesus, if His love has actually changed you, if being part of our squad means anything, and if you guys have any heart at all, if you care about anyone — do me a solid. Get on the same page, love each other, and be true ride-or-die friends. Don't be that person who's always trying to be the main character. Don't try to sweet-talk your way to the top. Instead, be humble and hype up your friends. Don't just look out for number one. Forget about yourself for a minute and help someone else out.","§He Took on the Status of a Slave","Your attitude should be the same as Jesus'. He was literally on the same level as God, but He didn't flex His power. He didn't cling to His top-tier status. Nah, when the time was right, He gave up all His perks, and basically became a servant. He became human! And He stayed human, which was a total glow-down for Him. He didn't ask for special treatment. He just lived a humble, obedient life and then died a humble, obedient death—the worst kind of death, too: crucifixion.","§God Lifted Him Up","Because He was so obedient, God gave Him the ultimate transformation and honored Him more than anyone or anything, ever. So now, everyone in heaven, on earth, and even those who died long ago and are buried, will bow down and worship Jesus. They'll all shout out that He's the boss, bringing major props to God the Father.","§Rejoicing Together","So, my friends, here's the deal. Just keep doing what you've been doing. When I was with you, you were all about listening and obeying. Now that I'm gone, you gotta step it up even more. Go hard in your faith, and be respectful and aware of God. That power you feel? That's God's power inside you, helping you do what makes Him happy.","§Shine Like Stars","Do everything readily and cheerfully — no complaining, no second-guessing allowed! Go out into the world uncorrupted, a breath of fresh air in this messed-up world. Show people what it's like to live a good life and know the living God. Be the light in the darkness, so when Jesus comes back, I can be proud of you. You'll be the proof that all my hard work wasn't for nothing.","§Rejoice With Me","And even if I get taken out right here, right now, I'll be happy to be part of the sacrifice of your faith. But hey, you gotta be happy for me too. Whatever you do, don't feel bad for me.","I'm planning to send Timothy to you guys soon, so he can give me the scoop on how you're all doing. That would be awesome. There's no one else like Timothy. He's a real one, and he actually cares about you. Most people are just in it for themselves and don't really care about Jesus' mission. But you know Timothy is legit. He's been like a son to me, and we've been spreading the message together. As soon as I know what's up with my situation here, I'll send him your way. And I'm hoping I'll be right behind him.","But for now, I'm sending Epaphroditus back to you. He's my boy, my partner in crime. You sent him to help me, and now I'm sending him to help you. He's been dying to see you all, especially since you heard he was sick. He wanted to let you know he's all good now. He almost died, for real, but God showed him mercy. And not just him, but me too. If he had died, it would have been another huge L for me.","So you see why I'm so stoked to send him back. When you see him all healthy and strong, you'll be so happy, and I'll be relieved. Give him a huge welcome and a big hug. People like him deserve all the respect. Remember how you guys started helping me but couldn't finish? Well, he finished the job, and he almost died doing it. What a legend."],"splits":[],"title":"How to Be a Real MVP","verseRanges":["1-4","1-4","5-8","5-8","9-11","9-11","12-13","12-13","14-16","14-16","17-18","17-18","19-24","25-27","28-30"]},{"changes":["Ch3: 기존 EN이 MSG 1절+반복 문단+2-6을 하나의 '1-4' 배지 문단으로 합병했던 것을 분리 — §To Know Him Personally(1), v1 본문(1), 반복 문단(1), 2-6 본문(2-6). MSG '### To Know Him Personally' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가","Ch3: MSG '### Focused on the Goal' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 12-14)","Ch3: 배지 수정 — '13-14'→'12-14' (MSG 문단 구분 기준)","Ch3: 2-6 문단에 MSG 'knife-happy circumcisers, I call them'과 'circumcised on the eighth day' 복원 (기존 'old-school rituals'만 있고 핵심 표현 누락)","Ch3: 7-9 문단에 MSG 'everything I once thought I had going for me is insignificant—dog dung' 복원","Ch3: 15-16 문단에 MSG 'God will clear your blurred vision—you'll see it yet!' 복원","Ch3: 17-19 문단에 MSG 'make their bellies their gods; belches are their praise' 복원 (기존 'all about their own desires'로 희석되어 있었음)"],"chapter":3,"confirmations_needed":["Ch3: MSG 1절의 'Be glad in God!' 문단과 'I don't mind repeating what I have written in earlier letters...' 문단을 합병하지 않고 2개 Teenz 문단(para 1, 2)으로 분리 유지함. 가독성상 하나로 합치는 것이 낫다고 판단되면 성욱 컨펌 후 합병 (merges 선언 필요)"],"merges":[],"msg_ranges":["1","1","1","2-6","7-9","10-11","12-14","12-14","15-16","17-19","20-21"],"paragraphs":["§To Know Him Personally","Alright, guys, that's about it. Be glad in God!","I don't mind saying again what I've already written — and I hope you don't mind hearing it again. Better safe than sorry — so here goes.","So here goes: steer clear of the barking dogs — those religious busybodies, all bark and no bite. I'd call them the knife-happy circumcisers; all they're into is appearances. The real believers are the ones the Spirit of God leads to work away at this ministry, filling the air with Christ's praise as we do it. We couldn't pull this off on our own, and we know it — even though we could list what plenty of people would call impressive credentials. You know my pedigree: a legitimate birth, circumcised on the eighth day; an Israelite from the elite tribe of Benjamin; a strict, devout follower of God's law; a fiery defender of my religion's purity, even to the point of persecuting the church; a meticulous observer of everything written in God's law Book.","But all that stuff I used to flex about? It's garbage. I've tossed it all out. Why? Because knowing Jesus is the ultimate prize. Compared to the epic privilege of knowing Jesus as my Master firsthand, everything I once thought I had going for me is insignificant — dog dung. I've dumped my old achievements so I can fully grab onto Christ and have him grab onto me. I don't want some weak, rule-based 'goodness.' I want the real, powerful kind that comes from trusting Christ — the kind that's straight from God.","I ditched all that lame stuff so I could really know Christ, feel his resurrection power, and even be part of his crew through the tough times, right up to the end. If there's a way to be in on the ultimate comeback—the resurrection—I'm all in.","§Focused on the Goal","Look, I'm not saying I'm perfect or that I've got it all figured out. But I'm on the journey, chasing after Christ, who amazingly chased after me first. Don't get it twisted, I'm no expert. But I'm laser-focused on the finish line, where God is calling us to be with Jesus. I'm running my race, and I'm not looking back.","So let's keep focused on that goal, those of us who want everything God has for us. If some of you have something else in mind, something less than total commitment, God will clear your blurred vision — you'll see it yet! Now that we're on the right track, let's stay on it.","Stick with me, friends. Keep track of those you see running this same course, headed for this same goal. There are many out there taking other paths, choosing other goals, and trying to get you to join them. I've warned you about them many times; sadly, I have to do it again. All they want is easy street. They hate Christ's cross. But easy street is a dead-end street. Those who live there make their bellies their gods — belches are their praise; all they can think of is their appetites.","But our story is way different. We're citizens of heaven! We're waiting for our Savior, the boss, Jesus Christ. He's going to give our regular bodies a miraculous transformation, making them awesome like his. He's got the power to put everything in its right place, and he's gonna make us whole."],"splits":[{"msg_range":"1","note":"MSG 1절 'Be glad in God!' 문단과 무번호 'I don't mind repeating what I have written in earlier letters...' 문단을 합병하지 않고 분리 유지 (원칙 2). § 헤더(para 0)는 배지 공유 규칙으로 커버","paras":[1,2]}],"title":"All-In for the Win","verseRanges":["1","1","1","2-6","7-9","10-11","12-14","12-14","15-16","17-19","20-21"]},{"changes":["Ch4: 기존 EN이 MSG 1절+2절+3절을 하나의 '1-3' 배지 문단으로 합병했던 것을 분리 — v1(1), §Pray About Everything(2), v2(2), v3(3). KO는 이미 분리되어 있었으므로 EN을 KO 구조에 맞춤","Ch4: 기존 EN이 MSG 4-5와 6-7을 하나의 '4-7' 배지 문단으로 합병했던 것을 분리 — 4-5와 6-7 (KO 구조와 일치)","Ch4: MSG '### Pray About Everything' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 2)","Ch4: MSG '### Content Whatever the Circumstances' 헤더를 § 문단으로 추가 (배지 10-14, 기존 invented 헤더 대체)","Ch4: 배지 수정 2건 — '15-16'→'15-17', '17-20'→'18-20' (MSG 문단 구분 기준)","Ch4: v1 문단에 MSG 'My dear, dear friends! I love you so much... Don't waver. Stay on track' 복원","Ch4: v2 문단에 MSG 'God doesn't want his children holding grudges' 복원","Ch4: v3 문단에 MSG 'Clement' 복원 (기존 EN에서 누락, KO에는 있었음)","Ch4: 8-9 문단에 MSG 'reputable, authentic, compelling'과 'the beautiful, not the ugly', 'what you heard and saw and realized' 복원","Ch4: 18-20 문단에 MSG 'And now I have it all—and keep getting more!' 복원 — 'the gifts keep coming' 추가","Ch4: null 배지였던 §Rejoice Always → '1', §Think About These Things → '4-5'로 수정"],"chapter":4,"confirmations_needed":[],"merges":[],"msg_ranges":["1","1","2","2","3","4-5","4-5","6-7","8-9","10-14","10-14","15-17","18-20","21-22","23"],"paragraphs":["§Rejoice Always","My dear, dear friends! I love you guys so much. I want the very best for you — you fill me with joy and make me so proud. Don't waver. Stay on track, steady in God.","§Pray About Everything","And hey, Euodia and Syntyche — you two need to squash your beef and make up. God doesn't want his kids holding grudges.","And, oh yes — Syzygus, since you're right there with them, do your best to help them work it out. These ladies worked for the Message hand in hand with Clement and me — total rockstars, right there with me and the rest of the OG squad, working as hard as any of us. Remember, their names are also in the Book of Life.","§Think About These Things","Keep the positive energy going with God 24/7. Seriously, get hyped about him! And be cool with everyone you meet; let them know you're on their team. The Boss could show up any second, so be ready!","Don't stress or worry about anything. Instead of panicking, just pray. Turn your worries into a conversation with God, and let him know what's up. Before you know it, you'll feel this awesome sense of peace, like everything's gonna be alright. It's a total game-changer when you let God's peace take over instead of letting worry run your life.","To wrap it up, my friends, you've gotta guard your thoughts. Focus on stuff that's real, honorable, reputable, authentic, compelling, and gracious. Think about the best, not the worst; the beautiful, not the ugly; stuff worth praising, not stuff worth cursing. Just copy what you learned from me — what you heard, what you saw, what clicked for you. If you do that, the God who lines everything up perfectly will bring some of that perfect harmony into your life.","§Content Whatever the Circumstances","I was so stoked to see you guys showing you care about me again. Not that you ever stopped, you just didn't have a chance to show it. But for real, it's not like I *needed* anything. I've learned the secret to being happy no matter what's going on. I'm good with a little and I'm good with a lot. I can handle being totally full or starving, having tons of cash or being broke. I can power through literally anything because of the One who gives me strength. But don't get me wrong, your help was a huge deal. It was awesome that you had my back when I was in a tight spot.","You guys in Philippi know the deal. When I first hit the road with the Message, you were the only church that had my back, the only ones who supported me. You even sent help more than once when I was in Thessalonica. I'm not saying this because I'm looking for a handout. I just want you to get the rewards that come from being generous.","And now I'm totally set — and the gifts keep coming! The stuff you sent with Epaphroditus was more than enough. It was like the best-smelling BBQ on the grill for God — he loved it. And you can bet that same God will take care of everything you need. His generosity is way bigger than yours, and it all comes through Jesus. Our God and Father gets all the glory forever and ever. Amen.","Say hi to all of God's people for me. My friends here say what's up. All the Christians here, especially the crew who work in Caesar's palace—the government headquarters—send their greetings.","May the incredible grace of our leader, Jesus Christ, be with you all, deep down in your spirit."],"splits":[],"title":"The No-Stress Guide to Life","verseRanges":["1","1","2","2","3","4-5","4-5","6-7","8-9","10-14","10-14","15-17","18-20","21-22","23"]}]